---
import { brand } from "@goliath/ui/brand";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Goliath Research Academy"
  description="Goliath Research Academy provides practical, notebook-based education in Python, statistics, and machine learning with concise explanations and executable examples."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Educational Offering · Available Today</p>
      <h1>Goliath Research Academy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Goliath Research Academy provides practical, notebook-based education in Python, statistics, and
        machine learning. Learners work through concise explanations and executable examples, with self-paced
        and instructor-assisted learning options.
      </p>
      <p class="prose">
        Our learning materials combine structured e-books, executable Jupyter notebooks, and real-world
        datasets—allowing students, entrepreneurs, and working professionals to study core mathematical and
        computational concepts and apply them directly in code. Courses and assessments are hosted on our
        learning portal at <a href={brand.academy}>academy.goliathresearch.com</a>.
      </p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href={brand.academy}>Go to academy.goliathresearch.com</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/partnerships/">Education partnerships</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="method-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="method-heading">How we teach</h2>
      <p class="prose">
        Instead of passive video lectures, Goliath Research Academy is built around active, hands-on
        computation:
      </p>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Concise Theory &amp; E-Books</h3>
          <p>
            Focused written explanations introduce statistical and machine-learning principles clearly,
            giving learners a durable reference without filler.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Executable Jupyter Notebooks</h3>
          <p>
            Every topic is paired with runnable Python notebooks so learners can inspect implementations,
            modify parameters, test edge cases, and experiment directly.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Real-World Examples &amp; Assessments</h3>
          <p>
            Worked examples and structured assessments connect theory to practical scientific, business, and
            engineering datasets.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <h3>Self-Paced &amp; Instructor-Assisted</h3>
          <p>
            Learners can study independently on their own schedule or work through material with instructor
            guidance in structured cohorts.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="curriculum-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="curriculum-heading">Subject areas &amp; courses</h2>
      <p class="prose">
        Our curriculum focuses on practical fluency in Python and its scientific computing ecosystem—chosen for
        its clear syntax, reproducible notebook workflows, and comprehensive libraries for statistics and
        machine learning.
      </p>
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <article class="card">
          <p class="kicker"><span class="chip status-live">Core Foundation</span></p>
          <h3>Practical Python &amp; Data Science</h3>
          <p>
            Python programming fundamentals, data structures, numerical computing, data cleaning, and
            visualization for reproducible data analysis.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="kicker"><span class="chip status-live">Core Course</span></p>
          <h3>Computational Statistics</h3>
          <p>
            Exploratory data analysis, probability distributions, sampling, hypothesis testing, confidence
            intervals, and simulation-based inference in Python.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="kicker"><span class="chip status-live">Core Course</span></p>
          <h3>Supervised Learning</h3>
          <p>
            Regression and classification models, regularization, decision trees and ensemble methods,
            cross-validation, and feature engineering on real-world problems.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <p class="kicker"><span class="chip status-live">Core Course</span></p>
          <h3>Unsupervised &amp; Deep Learning</h3>
          <p>
            Clustering, dimensionality reduction, representation learning, and neural network architectures
            for structured and unstructured datasets.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="band">
        <h2>For schools, training programs, and education partners</h2>
        <p>
          We work with educators, accelerators, and training organizations on course delivery, cohort
          instruction, and curriculum licensing. We are also exploring how our software platform can support
          practical learning and applied student projects.
        </p>
        <div class="cta-row">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/partnerships/">Discuss an education partnership</a>
          <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={brand.academy}>Visit academy.goliathresearch.com</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
